The rxd copy disables upstream standalone binaries in Cargo.toml; rxd invokes the
library directly. The marshal reader adds depth/object budgets and bounds collection
reservations against input bytes before parsing untrusted input. The source printer and
JSON serializer enforce output budgets before appending beyond the limit. Version
overrides reuse the cached magic table. Nested lambda/annotation/type-parameter
decompilation propagates detected incompleteness to the enclosing result.

Opt-in thread-local recovery phase timings separate index/decode/setup/walk/finalize/
generate; the adapter enables them only for `--perf`. Local changes also bound reference-expanded
object counts/depth, aggregate marshal byte
copies, quadratic integer conversion work and code-header counts; add strict
instruction/prefix/cache/exception validation; and provide bounded static code/constant/
reference evidence. No analyzed code is executed, and worker isolation is not an OS
sandbox. The imported Rust files are formatted with this workspace's rustfmt version so
`cargo fmt --all -- --check` passes. The upstream library opts out of the workspace Clippy
gate; rxd-pyc and the CLI adapter remain gated.

The rxd adapter now supplies explicit marshal object/reference-expansion/copy limits
for input-scaled CLI analysis, while default library loading retains its fixed limits.
Recursion, cycle rejection, code-header allocation hints and quadratic numeric-work
guards remain independent. Limits flow through both raw and header-bearing loaders.

Whole-module recovery now isolates unsupported function/class bodies as explicit
bytecode-comment fallbacks without discarding healthy siblings. Source labels reuse
static navigation's code-object preorder. Fallbacks retain raw instructions (including
prefix/cache bytes) and handlers; nested bodies whose enclosing bindings are unavailable
are rendered as isolated source comments. Malformed bytecode and resource exhaustion
remain errors, and generated fallback text uses the same bounded output writer.

Static navigation and reconstruction share embedded format resolution without an
adapter-maintained version whitelist. PEP 552 flags are validated in the shared header
reader. Original instruction spans/caps also handle variable-width legacy bytecode.
Comprehension filters follow their keep/skip branch graph; expanded calls retain the
versioned kwargs slot and list-to-tuple conversions. Internal stack-marker names cannot
be emitted as recovered source; unresolved bodies use the existing local fallbacks.

Selected reconstruction now preserves module-local code ordinals and optional PYZ
module namespaces. Non-root selections emit complete code-body fragments without
inventing the enclosing binding/defaults/decorators. Partial markers are scoped to
the selected subtree. BINARY_OP's subscription selector is handled before arithmetic
rendering; END_ASYNC_FOR's monitoring source offset is not a control-flow branch.

Upstream attribution and licensing remain unchanged. Any later local change belongs in
this vendored copy and should be documented here. Tests and corpus provenance are in
`tests/corpus/pyc/README.md` and `tests/fixtures/pyc/README.md`.
